# Auto-develop: let the image choose the starting adjustments.
#
# Same controls as develop.tgl, but the exposure, shadows and blacks sliders
# open where a measurement of the sensor data suggests instead of at zero.
#
# There is no second set of controls and no "auto mode" to leave. The
# measurement sets DEFAULTS, so:
#
#   - a slider you have not touched follows the suggestion
#   - a slider you drag stays exactly where you put it, through every re-run
#   - double-clicking one returns it to the suggestion
#
# Drop a raw file onto the "test" row. On a JPEG the measurement is skipped:
# a finished image has already had a tone curve applied, so its midtone says
# nothing about how the sensor was exposed.

src = image("test")

# auto_exposure is an option of params(), not a slider. It decides where the
# controls START; everything after that is an ordinary control you can drag.
developed = params(basic_adjust, auto_exposure = 1)(src)

display(src,       "1 original")
display(developed, "2 auto-developed")
